are your walls doing enough for you are  they smart enough do they spend way too  much time holding up the ceiling and  dividing your home into rooms shouldn't  they also be listening to you and  anticipating your every need  researchers have now found a way to make  the most responsive walls yet imagine  for example as you sit down on the sofa  the tv turns on lights dim when you  start watching something on your laptop  or Alexa lets you know that your kids  have turned on a portable videogame  system somewhere in the house this isn't  very difficult to do the first step is  converting a wall into a giant antenna  in this study researchers used tape to  make a grid on the wall then covered it  over with water-based paint containing  nickel they remove the tape which left  behind a pattern of metallic diamonds to  act as electrodes then they connected  two electrodes to a computer and painted  the wall with standard latex paint  hiding any signs of its new capabilities  now the wall can watch your every move  touching or moving an arm or limb close  to the wall changes the walls  electrostatic fields just as a finger  touching an iPad does it can tell if  you're exercising or heading for the  kitchen and if connected to your house  computer may one day turn on energizing  music or flip the kitchen lights on the  newly alert wall can even sense what you  are interacting with in the room lamps  laptops TVs and other electronic devices  all generate distinctive electromagnetic  fields eventually such walls which the  team created for $20 per square meter in  this study could feed this information  to electronic personal assistants or  your phone when you're not home  hopefully not the government  [Music]  [Music]
 

